	(text "Blackbox storage - W25Q128JV on its own SPI2 bus (STO-1)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.2 58.42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "22881883-cb49-488c-9af7-a7aac8e24151")
	)
	(text "STO-1 strapping. R8 10k on /CS: the die has no internal pull-up and the datasheet\nrequires /CS to track VCC at power-up, when the MCU pin is still high-Z.\nR9 / R10 10k on /WP (IO2) and /HOLD (IO3): NEVER hard ties - the IQ order code\nships with QE=1, which repurposes both pins as IO2/IO3, and the datasheet\nexplicitly forbids direct supply or ground ties in that state.\nOwn SPI bus, never shared with the IMU: logging writes must not contend with\nsensor reads. Plain SPI only, QUADSPI dropped (STO-3).\n\nFOOTPRINT: the KiCad symbol default (SOIC-8 3.9x4.9 mm) is WRONG for the JVSIQ\n208-mil wide body. Overridden to mark4-fc:SOIC-8_5.28x5.28mm_P1.27mm."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.2 139.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5897637d-0df2-4a2b-8b5d-4b602e4d8152")
	)
	(text "STO-5 throughput - why the bus is never the constraint, and the FIRMWARE rule.\nRequired sustained rate is 32.5 kB/s (65-byte record at 500 Hz, STO-2).\nThe W25Q128JV programs a 256-byte page in 0.7 ms typ / 3 ms max = 366 kB/s typ\nand 85 kB/s worst case, both above the requirement. SPI clock is irrelevant to\nwrites (50 MHz ceiling for plain 03h reads, 27 MHz chosen on SPI2).\nWhat matters is ERASE latency: a 4 KB sector erase stalls the die 45 ms typ,\nup to 400 ms max = 13 kB of backlog at the required rate.\nFIRMWARE MUST therefore buffer records in a RAM ring of 16 KB or more (cheap out\nof 256 KB) and erase AHEAD of the write head.\n\nSizing (STO-2): 16 MB is about 8 minutes of armed logging; logging only while\narmed is the intended policy. W25Q256JVSIQ (32 MB, same footprint) MAY be\nsubstituted at order time. Retrieval over USB CDC (STO-4), no SD card."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.2 170.18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
